## Third-party notices

This repository contains installation glue and documentation only. It does not
vendor or redistribute any third-party software or model weights; `install.sh`
downloads them from their upstream sources, which remain governed by their own
licences.

### MTPLX

The runtime UpinelAIOS drives is [MTPLX](https://github.com/youssofal/MTPLX),
licensed Apache-2.0 by Youssof Altoukhi, **with a mandatory attribution
requirement**. MTPLX's NOTICE states that any product, app, or service built on
it must display the following inside the product itself, somewhere a user can
see it (about screen, credits, settings, shipped docs, or a CLI startup banner):

> Powered by MTPLX
> https://github.com/youssofal/MTPLX

A mention in a repository or on a website does **not** satisfy this. If you
build something on UpinelAIOS that other people use, honour that requirement.

The exact wording and the full terms are in MTPLX's `NOTICE` file, which is
carried by every copy under Apache-2.0 section 4(d). The reference to MTPLX
above is an acknowledgement, not a substitute for reading it.

### Model weights

`sentence-transformers`-style licence inheritance does not apply here; the
weights are independent works:

| Artifact | Licence |
|---|---|
| `Qwen/Qwen3.8-27B` (base model) | Apache-2.0 |
| HauhauCS Aggressive uncensored fine-tunes | Apache-2.0 (per upstream model card) |
| `itrejomx/*-MTPLX-4bit` / `-6bit` MLX conversions | Apache-2.0 (community conversion; the author notes it is not an official HauhauCS release) |

The community conversions are exactly that — community conversions, not signed
upstream releases. Upstream HauhauCS releases carry Ed25519-signed manifests;
these do not. That is a provenance statement, not a legal one.

### Other components referenced

- [MLX](https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx) and
  [mlx-lm](https://github.com/ml-explore/mlx-lm) — MIT
- [llama.cpp](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp) — MIT (discussed in the
  research docs; not used by the default configuration)
- [Homebrew](https://brew.sh) — BSD-2-Clause

### Uncensored models

The default model is an uncensored fine-tune. It will comply with requests that
a safety-tuned model would refuse. You are responsible for what you serve and to
whom, and for the security of the LAN endpoint UpinelAIOS exposes.
